WEBVTT

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.960
Kiyokawa got beaten!

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.660
He's cutting in, Dori!

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.210
Damn!

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.720
Kuro, don't leave your man!

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.600
Katayama's coming!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.030
Don't let him pass!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.730
Bring it. I'll stop you!

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.360
Don't take the bait, Kuro! Watch out for Hauer!

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.870
A dink!

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.390
Tch...

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.860
Yeah, we've taken the lead!

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.370
Hey, Hauer!

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:51.630
That pass was just a loan. You'll have to return it!

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.740
What the hell, Hauer? You're supposed to pass the ball to me!

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.980
You've already scored today, so you're not allowed to shoot anymore.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.770
Yeah, it'll be only fair to us that way.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.020
Stop touching my hair!

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.530
Fantastic! That was fantastic, Sonoda!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.200
Ah, what a beautiful goal!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.020
I'm so touched that I feel like crying!

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.080
The 17th minute. Even the timing is perfect.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:31.550
They can't just sit back and defend now.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.550
And when they do that, we'll get even more chances.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:47.330
What a spiritual moment. Your aura has become even more marvelous!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.570
Stop it, Sonoda. We're still in the middle of a game.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.360
My apologies.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:01.830
Just keep an eye on Kubota's moves. Don't leave him off your sight.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.880
Giving instructions to Sugie?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.430
If you only plan to defend, you won't even get a draw...

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.090
Tatsumi Takeshi.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.730
Dori, I'm sorry.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.590
I'm not gonna let him do as he pleases from now on.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.430
There was nothing you could have done, Kuro.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.730
You're doing well.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.730
It's my fault. I lost out to Katayama.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.690
See, that's precisely what I was talking about.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.740
With you going up against the forwards, I feel uneasy indeed.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.490
Akasaki...

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.490
No one is asking you to win in every one-on-one situation,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.250
but you can at least slow him down, right?

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.230
Then we can come in and help out.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.260
To put it simply, you guys should go all out.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.500
Leave it at that. Let's go.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.520
Being pushed incredibly hard and conceding a goal...

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.020
that happened countless times last year.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.860
It's nothing to worry about now.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.530
Come on, let's attack.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.410
H-How's that kind of speech supposed to be inspire us?!

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.460
Where did you get those lines from, Prince?

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.160
That's not encouragement at all!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.420
Good.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.180
They don't look like they'll roll over just yet.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:40.750
Well they can't, since we aren't even halfway through the first half.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:51.940
It's quite laughable if you've think you've won, Dulfer.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.740
Oh my, quite a blow there for ETU.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.190
This match will be tough.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.680
Fujisawa, even you should know what this means.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.330
This is the beginning of the end for ETU.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:20.460
Are you trying to say that this club won't be able to cause an upset?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.890
Yes. No matter how hard they try, they'll only get a draw at most.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.220
They don't have the ability to score two goals in this kind of situation.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:34.910
To put it simply, they don't possess an ambitious streak in them.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:39.360
They lack a winning mentality, thus failing to make the right decisions when the time comes.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.860
Basically, there's a reason why a losing team can't win.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.530
Looks like it's still the same old story this season.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:52.680
This is the reality of the team you chose to follow around.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.670
I already know that, geez.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.570
Which is why I'm hoping...

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.360
for that magic spark from the manager.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:17.150
What will you do now, Monsieur Tatsumi?

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.030
Alright, it's about time, Natsu.

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:25.210
No problem! Let's go, Gino!

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.900
Prince passed the ball to Natsuki!

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.530
Go!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.230
We can't just sit back and absorb the pressure!

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.670
Let's turn this around, ETU!

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.910
It's merely one goal.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.650
So what?!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.910
I'll make it even in no time!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.890
I'm different today!

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:52.690
Teammates?

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:53.460
Where's my teammates?!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:54.680
They're all opponents!

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.310
Alright, we got it back!

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.150
Go get the second goal!

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.330
What were you doing, Natsuki?

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.530
You were dwelling on the ball for far too long!

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.030
Alright, let's go.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:09.530
Don't let him take it upfield!

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.780
We can't afford to let them control the game any longer!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:20.660
Nice, Murakoshi! Don't let them dominate!

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:21.660
Gino!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.320
It's long again. Another miscue?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:32.940
Tsubaki!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.760
I mustn't underestimate his legs.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.310
Nice one, Hiraga!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.720
I knew it.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:01.070
Gino's passes are usually very accurate...

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:03.130
but today they're way off.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.590
Whatever the case is,

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.800
it's causing Gino his form today.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.970
What are they waiting for?!

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:21.420
If they had gotten a shot in, then it would have looked like a real attack,

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.230
but they got countered instead!

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.390
Osaka may be well known for their offense,

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.740
but they also have national players that anchor the midfield and defense.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:34.370
The playmaker, Shimura.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.620
Captain, Hiraga.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.120
Centre-back, Terauchi.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.620
Left full-back, Komura.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:45.740
Those guys won't be beaten by a simple attack.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.370
We'll need to come up with an idea.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.130
Meanwhile, at the other end...

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.260
Got it!

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.790
... Having taken the lead, the momentum's with them.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.980
Get back! Slow them down!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.110
Let's keep pushing!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.120
Hauer's coming in, Kuroda!

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:16.900
They're still insisting on this mismatched pairing?

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.250
Well, I guess they have no other choice.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.130
Argh, they're attacking with Hauer again!

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:33.900
Your showtime's over! Brace yourself!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.760
You're so stuck-up despite your weird head!

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.360
Don't lose to him, Kuroda!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.000
To be honest,

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.770
I'm not really worried about Kuro.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:47.770
Hauer!

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:53.030
I have to shut that Akasaki up.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.860
Give it here already!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.030
Take this!

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.270
He won!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.750
Nice, Kuro!

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:16.880
Nice!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:25.020
Yup, that No.7 is interesting.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:30.770
Kubota!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.530
They claimed the loose ball again!

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:40.910
He always shows up at the worst time.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.170
Kubota...

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:49.990
We need to contain him, or we're done for.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.600
Kubota. I won't allow him to do as he pleases anymore.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.480
Where?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.490
Where will he send it?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.320
Sugie, don't let him!

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:25.770
Was it a foul?

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.500
No whistle!

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.330
It's up!

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.870
I'm gonna trounce you!

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:33.590
I won't let you!

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.030
It's high!

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.180
Kuroda!

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:42.970
It's too high!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:44.970
Alright.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.350
Behind them! It's Katayama!

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:51.640
Alright!

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.730
That was close!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.320
Too close!

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:05.130
Nice catch, Dori! That was a dangerous one.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.330
I was just lucky.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.990
We can't let them claim any more loose balls.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:15.320
Damn!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.670
That was scary.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:23.020
Nice save, Dori. He saw that it was for Katayama and not Hauer.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.100
However...

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.370
That guy is annoying, and he's quite sharp today.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.480
Haruhiko Kubota.

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:44.740
He's the youngest in the line-up for Osaka at the age of 20...

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:50.500
He was already a part of the national setup a few years ago, right?

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.330
How did he fare?

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.310
Umm... uhh...

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.520
He was mainly a bench warmer for the team,

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:03.760
and his performances were not eye-catching either.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:08.430
Plus, he was a defensive midfielder back then...

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.460
What's scary about Osaka's offense...

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.090
is that they don't lose the ball even in the opponent's half.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.780
First of all, their forwards retain the ball well.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:24.530
Also, they're able to communicate well and pass the ball around quickly.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.150
On the other hand, our defenders are unable to take the initiative,

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.730
thus we're forced to clear the ball hastily.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:37.370
The problem lies with those loose balls.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:41.130
Osaka's able to pick them up most of the time.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.970
That's the reason as to why their attacks never end.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:52.560
And the person who picks up those balls the most...

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.190
is that guy, Kubota.

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:00.190
That klutz?

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.880
The reason he's got great vision...

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.700
probably stems from the time when he was a defensive midfielder.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:13.120
His intuition however, might be a natural-born gift.

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.710
Not too bad, Dulfer.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:21.210
Making use of that immense talent in the forward position...

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:29.100
Unless you figure out how his talent as a forward came to be,

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:33.100
you won't be able to beat him, Sugie!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:41.770
Tatsumi told me to ignore my surroundings and keep an eye on Kubota only, but...

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:50.370
This guy's movements are so erratic, so unless I know what's going on around me, it'll be hard!

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.890
They're attacking again!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:55.870
Stop them!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.260
Calm down. Don't think too much about it!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:02.170
Though Kubota's a forward,

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:05.260
his main job is to send passes in from just behind the front line.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.590
I'll just have to prevent him from doing so!

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.100
I'm going to nail this one!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.470
Shut up already! Don't underestimate me!

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:19.020
Kiyo!

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.910
Oh, crap.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:21.650
Kubo!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.280
Kubota again!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:26.680
Uhh...

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.410
I won't allow you to pass it to Hauer!

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.280
Okay then,

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:35.600
I'll pass it to Hatake.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.420
There's some space for him to exploit.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.290
Here it comes!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.700
Huh?

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:46.300
Is this person not paying attention?

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.620
He keeps looking around.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.910
Seems like you don't get it, Sugie.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:56.150
This might be a good chance.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:01.060
Kubota was never meant to be a midfielder.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:04.370
He's a forward that scores goals.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:11.450
Hey, Hatake, give me the ball!

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.450
Shut up, Hauer!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.410
Will you pass the ball to me, Hatake?

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.210
A low and fast one.

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:24.700
The goal's right in front of me now.

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:32.670
I want to shoot... I want to shoot...

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.350
I can shoot.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.330
Kubota scored!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.630
The second goal!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:13.220
He did it, Sonoda! Kubota did it!

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.140
That's right, manager!

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:19.890
He shines the most when he scores a goal!

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.380
Well done, Kubo.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.650
Nice, Kubotan.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.990
Alright, nice goal, Kubota!

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:32.650
Aim for the big score again today!

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:35.910
Well done! Nice goal, Kubota.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.090
Like I expected...

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:41.910
This feeling's the best.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:47.780
When you score a goal, it feels like you're in heaven.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:52.060
This is why I won't quit.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.920
It makes me want to play forever.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:59.430
Nicely done, Kubota! It was a beautiful goal!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.730
Wonderful! Though his laughter is a bit creepy...

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:08.200
Yeah...

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:16.800
This reminds me of the day when I experimented him as a forward during pre-season training camp.

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:22.400
Two goals...

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.130
Kubota...

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.870
He's incredible. We're of the same age, too.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.800
It's over.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.060
Damn it!

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:41.970
Don't give up, ETU!

00:19:55.370 --> 00:20:00.120
It was like watching a butterfly emerge from a pupa.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:11.920
When he was a defensive midfielder, you could see that he's able to read the game well.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:19.020
However, he lacked stamina and hence wasn't regarded as an amazing player.

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:29.160
When I played him as a forward during a friendly, he became a totally different player.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.570
He sprayed around elegant, accurate passes.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.500
His off-the-ball movements were also well thought of.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:40.130
Everything he did was effective for scoring goals.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:50.000
That's why the ball keeps coming to him, whether it's being passed by a teammate or a loose one.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:21:00.050
That's when I ascertained that he is being loved by the ball.

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:08.620
By playing him as a forward, he could shine more than anyone else on the field.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:23.570
We have less than 10 minutes left in the first half.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.530
Attack already!

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:29.580
You can't let this half end without shooting even once!

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:36.090
There's no need to be afraid of Gino today.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:45.550
I've got to create something that'll give us a chance!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.400
Tsubaki!

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:49.310
Rampage your way towards the goal!

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:52.440
Tsubaki, pass the ball to me!

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:07.610
It's Kubota on the other end!

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:09.580
He's on a roll today!

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:13.860
It's fun.

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:16.800
It's so fun today!

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:20.340
We don't have time. Just boot the ball towards the goal!

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.550
Go forth and tussle it out!

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.560
Sera!

00:22:31.730 --> 00:22:34.310
Their defense is too tight!

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:38.820
One more time, get the ball and...

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:42.650
Nice one, guys!

00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:44.500
Keep it up in the second half!

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:46.090
Good job!

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:48.350
Let's destroy ETU!

00:24:15.710 --> 00:24:18.920
That's why, you guys! Go ahead and hit us!

00:24:19.170 --> 00:24:20.960
Are you guys enjoying the match?

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:24.840
Or is it just me?

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:28.160
Our big comeback is about to begin.
